WEBVTT

01:45.772 --> 01:49.109
For the time being,
he needs to stay like this.

01:49.192 --> 01:50.026
Yes, sir.

01:50.110 --> 01:53.279
Run antibiotics and painkillers in his IV.

01:53.863 --> 01:56.950
Replace his bandages every 12 hours.

01:57.033 --> 01:58.034
Yes, sir.

01:59.869 --> 02:02.038
Sorry about the sudden call.

02:02.622 --> 02:05.291
It's fine. I've done all I can.

02:05.792 --> 02:07.794
There will be some scarring.

02:08.503 --> 02:11.881
Also, his cervical spine
suffered heavy damage,

02:11.965 --> 02:13.925
but there are no neurological issues.

02:14.634 --> 02:17.178
His body is in good shape, after all.

02:17.262 --> 02:18.930
And what about this?

02:19.556 --> 02:22.433
You mean he did it
after losing consciousness?

02:22.517 --> 02:25.436
Yes, when he was out cold.

02:29.232 --> 02:32.527
You must know about this, Professor Payne.

02:32.610 --> 02:33.695
Know about what?

02:34.279 --> 02:37.198
Even when a human has lost consciousness...

02:37.782 --> 02:42.453
In fact, even after a human has lost
their life, they can still take action.

02:43.163 --> 02:47.292
This is a story that took place
under the special circumstances of war,

02:47.834 --> 02:48.960
but it's a true story.

02:50.253 --> 02:53.590
<i>Soldiers captured the soldiers
of their enemy's domain.</i>

02:54.299 --> 02:57.594
<i>Since it was wartime,
they were immediately sentenced to death.</i>

02:58.469 --> 03:01.139
<i>As they awaited their impending deaths,</i>

03:01.222 --> 03:03.433
<i>the commanding officer
of the captured troops</i>

03:03.516 --> 03:04.976
<i>made an outrageous proposal.</i>

03:05.560 --> 03:09.981
<i>He said, "After I'm beheaded,
I will pick up my head and run."</i>

03:10.857 --> 03:13.151
<i>"I will run down the line of my troops."</i>

03:13.651 --> 03:19.199
<i>"I want you to spare all the men
that I am able to run past."</i>

03:20.408 --> 03:22.744
<i>The enemy soldiers laughed uproariously.</i>

03:22.827 --> 03:24.746
<i>They said, "Go ahead and try if you can."</i>

03:25.496 --> 03:27.373
<i>He was immediately put to death.</i>

03:27.874 --> 03:29.500
<i>Unbelievably, he ran.</i>

03:30.168 --> 03:34.005
<i>He ran down the whole line of his troops
while carrying his own head.</i>

03:35.089 --> 03:36.007
What?

03:36.883 --> 03:38.009
It's a true story.

03:38.760 --> 03:42.013
In which case,
it's something Jack Hammer would do.

03:42.639 --> 03:47.518
Awake or asleep,
he's only ever pursued strength in life.

03:48.102 --> 03:51.022
<i>He is sure to have thought about
how else he could fight on</i>

03:51.648 --> 03:54.943
<i>after he was defeated and beyond.</i>

03:55.818 --> 03:57.487
<i>He must have engraved his plan</i>

03:57.570 --> 04:01.032
<i>into every corner
of every cell in his body.</i>

04:01.616 --> 04:04.285
It's something I'm sure Jack would do.

04:06.371 --> 04:09.040
The patient, Jack, is gone.

04:09.874 --> 04:11.042
You can't be serious!

04:12.168 --> 04:13.127
See?

04:17.674 --> 04:19.050
I'm sorry.

04:19.133 --> 04:22.053
I am sorry for leaving
in the middle of our fight.

04:23.721 --> 04:26.307
Let's continue!

04:27.392 --> 04:29.310
Let's continue!

04:30.645 --> 04:31.813
Let's continue!

04:32.480 --> 04:35.316
Let's continue!

04:36.943 --> 04:40.530
<i>He took five consecutive kicks
to the face from Jack's powerful legs.</i>

04:41.739 --> 04:45.910
<i>How much damage had Pickle suffered?
In actuality, not very much.</i>

04:47.078 --> 04:50.832
<i>Before, he had fought daily
with beasts hundreds of times his weight.</i>

04:51.874 --> 04:54.085
<i>Even though Jack had powerful legs,</i>

04:54.836 --> 04:57.088
<i>and even though he had powerful fists,</i>

04:57.714 --> 05:00.591
<i>his weight and Jack's weight
were nearly the same.</i>

05:01.342 --> 05:04.095
<i>So, why is he running?</i>

05:05.054 --> 05:08.433
<i>It was no longer an issue
of strength nor might.</i>

05:09.142 --> 05:11.352
<i>I've never seen anyone
like this man before.</i>

05:11.436 --> 05:15.189
<i>A man who won't die after being killed,
who won't die after he's dead.</i>

05:16.441 --> 05:20.862
<i>That one, and that one, and that one,</i>

05:21.571 --> 05:23.614
<i>when they died, it was all over.</i>

05:24.282 --> 05:27.118
<i>Even that one didn't try to charge at him.</i>

05:28.328 --> 05:30.121
<i>That's the rule here, isn't it?</i>

05:30.955 --> 05:34.125
<i>Jack Hanma, a truly uncommon fighter.</i>

05:35.168 --> 05:36.961
<i>He intentionally overworked his body.</i>

05:37.045 --> 05:40.173
<i>He ingested an obscene amount of drugs,
consequences be damned.</i>

05:41.049 --> 05:45.136
<i>He was willing to have all four limbs
cut off for bone-lengthening surgery.</i>

05:45.720 --> 05:48.890
<i>With no expectations for the future,
he lived purely for the present.</i>

05:48.973 --> 05:52.143
<i>When you think about it,
all of it is the ultimate in unnatural.</i>

05:52.226 --> 05:54.395
<i>None of it exists in the natural world.</i>

05:55.313 --> 05:57.273
<i>Like how people dread ghosts,</i>

05:58.066 --> 06:00.401
<i>and like how people
avoid the inexplicable,</i>

06:01.069 --> 06:04.906
<i>Pickle also feared whatever it was
that made Jack what he is.</i>

06:05.698 --> 06:09.911
<i>However, a person can only
turn their back on fear for so long.</i>

06:10.620 --> 06:12.997
<i>Exactly two minutes
after the fight had begun,</i>

06:14.415 --> 06:17.919
<i>his pride at being undefeated
in the Cretaceous was ignited.</i>

06:41.442 --> 06:45.154
<i>It was a defeat that he himself sought.
One he himself could acknowledge.</i>

06:45.905 --> 06:49.826
<i>Even if he did want to acknowledge it,
the coma he was in was too deep.</i>

06:50.701 --> 06:54.163
<i>It was the second time in his life
he had lost twice in a day.</i>

07:02.672 --> 07:04.924
Oh! Thank goodness.

07:05.007 --> 07:06.592
You are quite strong.

07:09.178 --> 07:12.014
This is the hospital
you were in this morning.

07:12.098 --> 07:13.182
You're back again.

07:17.019 --> 07:18.104
Don't you dare.

07:18.813 --> 07:20.606
You've already done enough.

07:23.192 --> 07:27.155
You fought with
that unparalleled cultural treasure,

07:27.238 --> 07:30.616
and both times you injured each other.
There won't be a third time.

07:30.700 --> 07:34.120
You've done enough, Jack Hammer.

07:40.209 --> 07:42.378
Where do you think you're going, Jack?

07:46.466 --> 07:50.928
Jack, I know painfully well
what you're feeling.

07:51.971 --> 07:56.893
Not because we're brothers,
but because we were both born warriors.

07:57.810 --> 07:59.395
That's why I know it's over.

08:02.106 --> 08:02.940
Jack!

08:04.609 --> 08:08.738
You, you're through as a fighter!

08:12.033 --> 08:15.912
<i>Unless one acknowledges their defeat,
they cannot be a loser.</i>

08:17.079 --> 08:21.918
<i>This idea of Jack's had been elevated
to the point of being his creed.</i>

08:22.710 --> 08:26.714
<i>However, after being forced
into unconsciousness a second time,</i>

08:26.797 --> 08:30.009
<i>what Pickle did, what was done to Jack,</i>

08:31.594 --> 08:33.804
<i>when Jack heard about it,</i>

08:34.472 --> 08:38.976
<i>nothing could be more disgraceful to him,
a warrior.</i>

08:40.478 --> 08:42.563
<i>Pickle carried Jack
from where they fought.</i>

08:43.356 --> 08:45.566
<i>He carried Jack very carefully.</i>

08:46.484 --> 08:49.820
<i>He handled him very carefully,
so as not to drop him</i>

08:50.655 --> 08:53.324
<i>or cause him any more injury.</i>

08:54.242 --> 08:57.286
<i>But why?
Soon, the reason would become clear.</i>

08:58.579 --> 09:00.081
<i>Of all things,</i>

09:00.831 --> 09:05.169
<i>Pickle was attempting to preserve
giant Jack Hammer to be eaten later.</i>

09:06.546 --> 09:08.589
You know what that means, Jack, right?

09:09.465 --> 09:12.593
He didn't bury you.
He handled you carefully.

09:13.636 --> 09:15.680
Not as an enemy, but as a meal.

09:17.223 --> 09:19.183
You know what that means, right?

09:25.773 --> 09:29.402
He says it's not fair now, so he'll wait.

09:29.485 --> 09:33.489
He said he'll wait however many days
it takes until the time comes.

09:34.073 --> 09:35.992
The problem is where he's doing it.

09:37.159 --> 09:39.453
He's right in front of him.

09:39.537 --> 09:42.331
Two men are facing each other
in the underground arena

09:42.415 --> 09:44.500
without spectators.

09:46.085 --> 09:50.506
He says he'll wait days, without eating.

09:55.886 --> 09:58.014
Do you think Baki can win?

10:00.600 --> 10:03.227
<i>The great fighter Sea King Retsu
was defeated.</i>

10:03.311 --> 10:06.147
<i>The reborn Katsumi Orochi was crushed.</i>

10:06.230 --> 10:09.025
<i>Even the beast Jack Hammer was...</i>

10:09.650 --> 10:11.027
You know, Yujiro,

10:11.652 --> 10:14.280
as far as I know, those three...

10:17.241 --> 10:20.536
they'd be the most powerful warriors
of the Earth Defense Force.

10:21.120 --> 10:23.247
Of these three,
it would be no surprise at all

10:23.331 --> 10:26.542
if any of them defeated Baki Hanma.

10:30.129 --> 10:32.548
That's <i>mefun</i> from Hokkaido.

10:33.132 --> 10:35.259
<i>Shiokara</i> made of salmon innards.

10:36.385 --> 10:38.804
Oh, you're quite the gourmet.

10:39.847 --> 10:40.806
It's my favorite.

10:41.599 --> 10:43.059
Oh, really?

10:45.186 --> 10:49.315
Like I was saying, the fighting power
of those three is on par with Baki--

10:49.398 --> 10:50.816
Mitsunari!

10:52.401 --> 10:55.946
There's one thing that Baki's got
that those three don't.

10:56.030 --> 10:58.741
Baki's undeniably got my blood.

10:59.283 --> 11:01.327
He's clearly of Hanma lineage.

11:01.410 --> 11:04.330
What? But Jack's also got yours.

11:04.914 --> 11:06.290
It runs thin in him.

11:06.916 --> 11:08.834
Thin?

11:09.418 --> 11:13.339
Seeing the results, it's clear.
It runs thin in him.

11:15.925 --> 11:20.346
You mean if he doesn't win,
your blood runs thin in him? Good grief.

11:22.932 --> 11:24.850
Your pride dumbfounds me.

11:26.185 --> 11:27.603
Incidentally, Ogre,

11:28.562 --> 11:30.106
don't you want to fight him?

11:34.694 --> 11:37.196
Don't you worry, Mitsunari.

11:37.279 --> 11:40.366
Don't give up on Baki Hanma just yet.

11:41.283 --> 11:43.369
They're destined to fight eventually!

11:45.454 --> 11:48.290
Whoever's left standing, I'll eat them.

11:50.418 --> 11:52.253
I've heard that animals in the wild

11:53.087 --> 11:56.716
can survive for long periods
without eating.

11:57.842 --> 12:02.763
But Pickle must certainly have reached
his limit, don't you think, Payne?

12:03.973 --> 12:09.812
<i>I won't stand anyone else
fighting Pickle except me.</i>

12:10.354 --> 12:12.314
<i>I want to do it before anyone else.</i>

12:13.190 --> 12:16.110
<i>Dammit. That's my problem.</i>

12:16.610 --> 12:20.114
<i>Not just before anyone else,
I should have been here from the start.</i>

12:20.740 --> 12:22.032
<i>I should just be here.</i>

12:22.783 --> 12:25.035
<i>Say, Pickle, let's stay like this</i>

12:25.995 --> 12:27.538
<i>until the time comes.</i>

12:27.621 --> 12:29.540
<i>Until then, we'll stay like this,</i>

12:30.875 --> 12:33.878
<i>breathing the same air,
sleeping when we're sleepy,</i>

12:33.961 --> 12:35.546
<i>eating when we're hung--</i>

12:36.130 --> 12:38.048
<i>Oh! That's right!</i>

12:39.049 --> 12:42.553
<i>This guy's gonna eat.
He's gonna eat me when he's hungry!</i>

12:42.636 --> 12:45.222
No, that problem's been solved.

12:47.767 --> 12:51.312
We've already got the food
that Pickle killed.

12:53.898 --> 12:57.401
<i>You mean that T-Rex
that's preserved in the U.S.?</i>

12:58.569 --> 13:00.821
There was a lot of it.

13:01.405 --> 13:02.656
Several tons.

13:05.034 --> 13:09.205
But that's not beef or pork.
It's an important cultural--

13:09.288 --> 13:11.081
It doesn't belong to anyone.

13:11.165 --> 13:15.836
Pickle obtained that himself,
and put his life on the line to do so.

13:16.504 --> 13:19.465
That dinosaur corpse is
important cultural property.

13:19.548 --> 13:21.300
There's no debate about that.

13:21.383 --> 13:24.345
However, it's no replacement for Pickle.

13:24.929 --> 13:26.972
<i>He's alive, you see.</i>

13:33.437 --> 13:34.730
What's that?

13:37.942 --> 13:39.610
This thing's priceless.

13:39.693 --> 13:42.822
It's 40 kilos of real Tyrannosaurus meat.

13:44.198 --> 13:46.408
This is probably far enough.

13:46.492 --> 13:48.619
It's only 100 meters to the arena.

13:49.245 --> 13:52.373
Let's get out of here.
We'll be killed if he finds us here.

13:56.877 --> 13:58.379
What? Really?

14:00.923 --> 14:01.966
Pickle...

14:06.971 --> 14:09.139
You're totally eating, man!

14:13.018 --> 14:14.895
But that's raw, right?

14:14.979 --> 14:16.397
It's got sand on it too.

14:20.067 --> 14:22.403
Well, if you insist.

14:32.496 --> 14:34.665
You know, this is actually really good.

14:36.041 --> 14:37.418
Thanks for this, man.

14:40.004 --> 14:42.423
This is totally great.
What kind of meat is this?

14:44.967 --> 14:46.760
I'm stuffed!

14:50.306 --> 14:51.265
<i>Wait.</i>

14:52.725 --> 14:54.935
<i>If Pickle's full...</i>

14:59.523 --> 15:00.482
<i>will he even fight?</i>

15:01.525 --> 15:03.944
He won't fight, never again.

15:04.820 --> 15:09.158
Our team is currently
achieving great results.

15:10.784 --> 15:11.952
Results?

15:12.036 --> 15:15.247
Using the T-Rex meat
that's been preserved,

15:15.331 --> 15:18.459
we're working on using biotech
to reproduce it.

15:18.542 --> 15:21.211
Is that kind of thing even possible?

15:22.338 --> 15:27.468
Two years, the time it will take
for Pickle to consume all the T-Rex meat,

15:27.551 --> 15:30.971
is plenty of time to go
from testing to production.

15:31.055 --> 15:33.974
Pickle will never starve.

15:34.808 --> 15:36.977
If he's satisfied, then...

15:37.061 --> 15:39.730
Naturally, he won't need to fight.

15:39.813 --> 15:44.485
Just like we normal people,
who enjoy dessert after dinner.

15:47.571 --> 15:49.490
VIRTUE

15:56.080 --> 15:58.999
That's what Payne says.

16:01.585 --> 16:04.463
Payne is a scholar.

16:04.546 --> 16:06.757
He can't help but think that way.

16:06.840 --> 16:07.841
I see.

16:07.925 --> 16:10.886
Then what kind of ideas
would a yakuza have?

16:10.970 --> 16:13.263
What would Fighting Master
Kaoru Hanayama think?

16:13.347 --> 16:17.726
Though it wasn't for very long,
I was in physical contact with Pickle.

16:18.352 --> 16:19.353
Really?

16:19.436 --> 16:22.481
You mean you fought him? When? Where?

16:22.564 --> 16:24.024
It was just a pushing match.

16:24.108 --> 16:27.069
Damn! I wish I could've seen that!

16:27.152 --> 16:30.114
A pushing match
between Hanayama and Pickle!

16:30.197 --> 16:32.282
So, who won?

16:32.866 --> 16:35.619
Don't you worry, Noble Elder.

16:35.703 --> 16:37.287
Pickle's on our side.

16:37.371 --> 16:38.622
Our side?

16:42.876 --> 16:44.753
Whether he eats you or not,

16:45.337 --> 16:47.339
he loves a good contest of strength.

16:49.883 --> 16:52.720
Just like when the finest of men
and the finest of women

16:52.803 --> 16:54.805
are in the same room...

16:57.725 --> 16:59.309
<i>they can't remain strangers.</i>

17:00.602 --> 17:04.314
<i>The admirers face one another
and their gazes come together.</i>

17:04.940 --> 17:06.483
<i>They're in a fighting arena.</i>

17:07.026 --> 17:08.819
<i>There's no way nothing will happen.</i>

17:11.405 --> 17:13.574
<i>It was a spur-of-the-moment idea.</i>

17:14.491 --> 17:18.078
<i>But the provocation was way too effective.</i>

17:19.455 --> 17:21.582
<i>Even though he was already very satisfied,</i>

17:22.458 --> 17:24.835
<i>and even though he felt at peace.</i>

17:25.794 --> 17:28.088
<i>Pickle couldn't understand language,</i>

17:28.172 --> 17:30.841
<i>but his wrath was set aflame
by this obvious provocation.</i>

17:41.810 --> 17:43.854
<i>It wasn't the least bit violent,</i>

17:43.937 --> 17:46.231
<i>and was actually quite gentle,</i>

17:46.315 --> 17:48.942
<i>but the soft approach</i>

17:49.026 --> 17:51.987
<i>deeply injured Pickle in a way
he never had been before.</i>

17:54.865 --> 18:00.079
<i>It was the third UFK tournament
in Charlotte, North Carolina, U.S.A.</i>

18:01.246 --> 18:04.917
<i>Lorion Grassy had easily won
the tournament the first time.</i>

18:05.626 --> 18:07.961
<i>He was the top seed by far.</i>

18:08.462 --> 18:11.465
<i>His opponent in the first match
was a mysterious fighter.</i>

18:11.548 --> 18:12.633
<i>His name was Timo.</i>

18:13.258 --> 18:17.387
<i>Lorion was predicted to win instantly,
but it was a shockingly tough fight.</i>

18:18.222 --> 18:20.140
<i>Lorion barely won the match,</i>

18:20.641 --> 18:24.394
<i>and was so exhausted that he lost
his sight. He forfeited his second fight.</i>

18:25.312 --> 18:28.565
<i>Timo had fought an incredible fight
that exceeded expectations.</i>

18:28.649 --> 18:31.401
<i>When asked about the secret
to his superhuman power, he said...</i>

18:31.485 --> 18:35.030
That jerk slapped my cheek! Gently!

18:35.114 --> 18:37.116
So lightly, it was condescending!

18:48.627 --> 18:51.547
Pickle, thank you.

18:52.131 --> 18:56.051
You understood that I insulted you.

18:56.718 --> 18:58.804
Pickle, you've evolved.

18:59.721 --> 19:02.683
<i>For the first time since you were born,</i>

19:02.766 --> 19:06.895
<i>you're fighting not to eat,
but to defend your pride!</i>

19:14.695 --> 19:16.071
It's just begun.

19:16.738 --> 19:20.576
The most powerful male of the era
of the dinosaurs versus Baki Hanma.

19:20.659 --> 19:23.078
Whoa! He's knocked him down!

19:23.787 --> 19:26.081
It was a ferocious high roundhouse kick.

19:26.165 --> 19:29.084
It was an extremely fruitful
and majestic kick,

19:30.043 --> 19:32.337
and very typical
of a first blow from Baki.

19:32.921 --> 19:34.840
Pickle's appetite has been satisfied.

19:35.674 --> 19:37.551
I'm sure Baki will communicate to him

19:38.510 --> 19:41.346
that fighting itself is a culture,

19:42.890 --> 19:45.851
not a means for hunting or eating.

19:46.935 --> 19:50.606
Surely, Baki will convey to him
that this fight is to defend his pride,

19:51.315 --> 19:53.275
to protect his dignity.

19:54.443 --> 19:56.445
He will communicate this kindly,

19:56.528 --> 19:59.323
and in terms that couldn't be
any easier to understand.

20:05.954 --> 20:08.123
<i>Kill or be killed!</i>

20:08.832 --> 20:10.042
<i>It's not about that.</i>

20:12.502 --> 20:14.546
<i>Eat or be eaten!</i>

20:15.172 --> 20:17.049
<i>It's not about that, Pickle.</i>

20:17.132 --> 20:20.052
Does he intend to kill him?!

20:20.636 --> 20:24.056
<i>What we're gonna do
isn't a fight to the death.</i>

20:24.973 --> 20:27.559
<i>We don't have to take each other's lives.</i>

20:28.185 --> 20:30.562
<i>There's no need to go that far.</i>

20:30.646 --> 20:33.232
He's gonna end it!

20:33.315 --> 20:35.359
No. No, he's not.

20:46.411 --> 20:47.829
<i>Aw, man!</i>

20:47.913 --> 20:49.831
Is he gonna go to the ceiling?!

20:51.667 --> 20:53.835
<i>You get the picture, Pickle.</i>

20:53.919 --> 20:56.380
<i>That's the way.</i>

20:56.463 --> 20:59.591
That's exactly what you've gotta do
in a contest of strength.

21:01.176 --> 21:04.263
<i>They're high, too high!
They'll never break their fall.</i>

21:04.346 --> 21:06.598
<i>They're 20... No, 30 meters high!</i>

21:06.682 --> 21:08.100
Whoa!

21:08.183 --> 21:10.352
<i>Oh shit, they're way too high.</i>

21:10.435 --> 21:11.603
<i>This won't end well.</i>

21:13.438 --> 21:16.608
<i>Wow, we're so close to the lights.</i>

21:17.192 --> 21:18.360
<i>We're so high!</i>

21:19.069 --> 21:20.362
<i>Oh, they're here.</i>

21:20.445 --> 21:21.863
<i>This is insane.</i>

21:21.947 --> 21:23.115
<i>The ground...</i>

21:43.719 --> 21:45.220
They're standing!

21:45.721 --> 21:46.555
<i>Ludicrous!</i>

21:47.139 --> 21:52.144
<i>Pickle maybe, but for Baki
to be able to stand up immediately after?</i>

21:53.020 --> 21:53.979
<i>Impossible...</i>

21:54.730 --> 21:58.650
<i>Is Baki Hanma
really that tough of a warrior?</i>

22:06.742 --> 22:08.660
<i>He's closing in on him.</i>
